# Requital VPS reverse proxy — canonical copy of /etc/caddy/Caddyfile.
#
# Captured verbatim from the live VPS (187.52.114.246:/etc/caddy/Caddyfile) on
# 2026-08-31. The only additions in this repo copy are these leading comment
# lines, which Caddy ignores. Deploy instructions: deploy/README.md.
#
# Blocks, in Caddy's precedence order:
#   {...}                     global: ACME email + on-demand-TLS `ask` hook.
#                             `ask` -> http://localhost:3000/domains/verify
#                             (the backend DomainsController). Consulted only by
#                             the `https://` catch-all below.
#   requital.io, www.         301 redirect to admin.requital.io.
#   admin.requital.io         -> :3001 (admin app). Cert: automatic (HTTP-01).
#   api.requital.io           -> :3000 (NestJS backend). Cert: automatic.
#   *.requital.io             -> :3002 (storefront). Cert: ONE Cloudflare DNS-01
#                             wildcard (needs CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN from
#                             /etc/caddy/caddy.env). NOT on-demand TLS — every
#                             subdomain shop rides this proactively-issued
#                             wildcard.
#   https://                  catch-all for connected custom domains -> :3002.
#                             Cert: on-demand TLS, gated by the `ask` hook above.
#                             This is the ONLY block that uses on-demand TLS.
#
# CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN lives in /etc/caddy/caddy.env (systemd EnvironmentFile,
# mode 600) — a secret, NOT committed here, same as backend/.env.

{
	email admin@requital.io
	on_demand_tls {
		ask http://localhost:3000/domains/verify
	}
}

requital.io, www.requital.io {
	redir https://admin.requital.io{uri} 301
}

admin.requital.io {
	reverse_proxy localhost:3001
}

api.requital.io {
	reverse_proxy localhost:3000
}

*.requital.io {
	tls {
		dns cloudflare {env.CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN}
	}
	reverse_proxy localhost:3002
}

https:// {
	tls {
		on_demand
	}
	reverse_proxy localhost:3002
}
